id: pmc-closed-locale-ties
title: Decide locale-independent ties for completed changelog entries
description: "Equal completion timestamps retain the existing locale-sensitive title/ID order. Verified main-build goldens differ between English and Swedish locales for accented titles, and code-unit ordering would change existing completed output. The current non-lifecycle write-stability task explicitly preserves completed ordering. Decide a separate compatibility policy for cross-locale completed ties, with corpus and projection coverage before changing the behavior."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags[2]: follow-up,ordering
created_at: "2026-11-06T20:26:54.672Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T20:32:04.748Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: "Document compatibility policy for equal completion timestamps; compare English and Swedish baseline goldens; retain completion timestamp precedence and release placement; cover Markdown, JSON and summaries."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T20:32:04.731Z",codex-sol,"Verified the original main build in English and Swedish locales: equal completion timestamps order underscore/dash and lowercase/uppercase title or ID ties using the existing locale comparator, with accented titles moving relative to z between locales. The current write-stability change deliberately preserves this behavior under its scope restriction. A dedicated compatibility regression captures both baseline ID orders and passes in the 10-test linked suite. Any future completed-tie policy change must explicitly update this compatibility contract."
